      "writtenOn": "2023-05-16T07:22:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Cole added this code in https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/2316418 for multi-product builds with Bazel. i.e. the idea that one can build for multiple products in a single bazel invocation. We initially planned for building multi-arch mainline modules, but the idea can be extended to more use cases, especially with RBE supporting wide graphs. Details: b/249685973\n\nPlease do not submit this unless you have a clear alternative plan on helping Bazel achieve the above, along with breaking down modules into product dependent and independent portions for the existing build system (without Bazel), which IMO is non-trivial given the complexity of the migration.",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42a7fdad_e7daad6e",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-16T07:59:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure. This isn\u0027t intended to be submitted as is. It was to augment what we are thinking. So, thanks for reviewing.\n\nMay I make a counter proposal? Instead of using the same word \"common\" for all targets, can we use an identifier which encode some of the axis we care about? For example, `\u003carch\u003e[-\u003c2nd_arch\u003e]`.",
      "parentUuid": "10ca06d6_46b5c8d6",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c01a8da_de29a4f4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-16T07:59:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch! The existence of multiplatform builds totally fell out of my brain 😞",
      "parentUuid": "10ca06d6_46b5c8d6",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4c42dbb_fab9d637",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1514900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-16T08:49:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just using arch identifier (or some other axis) isn\u0027t sufficient to map to all product variables that can influence the build, which currently is represented only by the $TARGET_PRODUCT and nothing lower-level than that.",
      "parentUuid": "7c01a8da_de29a4f4",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d2c3e75_deca51db",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-16T12:49:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doesn\u0027t `DeviceProduct()` represent the entire build config either? We can override some of the build configs via `SOME_CONFIG\u003dvalue m`. Furthermore, the config of the same product could change over time.",
      "parentUuid": "c4c42dbb_fab9d637",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9189cc47_656bb262",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-16T18:01:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Will this cl even reduce the number of outputs? They\u0027ll still be qualified by their config hash which will change even if the prefix doesn\u0027t change.\n\nEnvironment variables are currently load-time, so they\u0027ll cause reanalysis and rebuilding in bazel. But we can switch them to be build settings which would be more configuration orthogonal to the product, and then they\u0027ll go to a folder with the same product name but a different config hash.",
      "parentUuid": "4d2c3e75_deca51db",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "572b6fc0_4b24a3fc",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1413436
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T02:21:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Intention of this change is to reduce # of build modules when lunch target has been changed into similar item (such as aosp_cf_phone to aosp_cf_foldable), so this is not about reducing # of outputs.\n\nWhat I\u0027m a bit confused from here is that, soong intermediates are target product agnostic as we discussed from b/282118864, while multiplatform builds will generate multiple variants from a single build. Are we expected to trigger multiplatform build with soong? or is it only for the bazel-only build scenario?",
      "parentUuid": "9189cc47_656bb262",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "124b2b63_b1c0cb70",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T06:59:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This setup is for Soong-less pure Bazel builds. It\u0027s nice because then one can build a full Mainline module (supporting every architecture) in a single invocation, no laborious re-analysis required, which makes build times *much* faster.",
      "parentUuid": "572b6fc0_4b24a3fc",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99bca11b_17b74a7f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T07:01:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if we make this to have zero side effect for the Bazel-only builds, would this idea be acceptable then?",
      "parentUuid": "124b2b63_b1c0cb70",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8db74ff7_4e4b9f9d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1514900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T07:22:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we all take a pause on this change and regroup on a design doc that spells out the clear benefits vs costs, who this impacts, and alternatives considered? \n\nI\u0027m mostly concerned that we\u0027re going to be stuck discussing this without a clear understanding on what either teams are trying to (ultimately) do. We should be more aligned.",
      "parentUuid": "99bca11b_17b74a7f",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed0350d4_214e8716",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T07:23:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not worried about Bazel at the moment.\n\nI\u0027m worried about ensuring that ostensibly product-agnostic modules are really product-agnostic because if you don\u0027t that, reusing modules built for one product for the build of another one is unsafe.\n\nHow about y\u0027all write up a design doc about how you think reuse of product-agnostic modules would work, then we discuss the necessary steps there?",
      "parentUuid": "99bca11b_17b74a7f",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "885092d7_70c0c8be",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T07:34:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sounds good. I don\u0027t want to rush. We will come back to you with a short design doc.\n\nJust one comment:\n\n\u003e reusing modules built for one product for the build of another one is unsafe.\n\nOf course, it\u0027s unsafe - if the builds were actually different. Even with this change, if the builds were actually different, they would have been rebuilt (i.e. clobbered, because they are built at the same path), which is bad for performance but is still safe.\n\nDo you think it would be considered unsafe even if the build rules (not only for the module itself, but also for all of its transitive dependencies) are exactly the same? We do the same for RBE, and we thought that this can be considered as a \"local\" cache.",
      "parentUuid": "ed0350d4_214e8716",
      "revId": "fd5c0b5f59312693b31aee00ae5f629178a86fca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
